Product conservation emphasizes preserving, maintaining, and extending the functional and aesthetic life of existing products rather than replacement with new items. Conservation strategies encompass proper care education, protective accessories, preventive maintenance systems, and storage solutions that prevent degradation. From a circular economy perspective, conservation represents the highest-value end-of-life strategy by keeping products in use the longest with minimal additional resource consumption. Design for conservation includes robust materials, simple maintenance requirements, and documentation that helps users protect their possessions.